' 10. Send a message to a learner
' Use case: Send direct message, «extend» Report a message (Friends & communicate) · Actors: Learner A, Learner B
'
' Design patterns:
'   - Observer (publish/subscribe): publish(B, "inbox") reaches B's open tabs through the RealtimeBus
'   - Chain of responsibility: authenticate → rate limit before the controller
'   - Unit of work: message saved with the conversation's update in one transaction
'   - Repository
' Lifelines use BCE stereotypes: «boundary» screens and outside services, «control» use-case logic (controllers,
' services, and the adapter interfaces in front of outside services), «entity» stored data (repository, stores);
' the database keeps its own symbol.
@startuml 10 Send a message
title 10. Send a message to a learner
autonumber
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true

actor "Learner A" as A
boundary "Web app A" as WebA
control "Communication\ncontroller" as Ctrl
control "Direct-message\nservice" as Svc
entity "Repository" as Repo
database "Database" as DB
control "Live updates\n(RealtimeBus)" as Bus
boundary "Web app B" as WebB
actor "Learner B" as B

A -> WebA : open a conversation with B
WebA -> Ctrl : POST /api/messages/conversations (B's username)
Ctrl -> Svc : startDirect()
Svc -> Repo : find the pair's conversation, or create it (one per pair)
Ctrl --> WebA : conversation

A -> WebA : write and send
WebA -> Ctrl : POST /api/messages/conversations/:id/messages
note over Ctrl : «Chain of responsibility»\nauthenticate → rate limit
Ctrl -> Svc : sendDirect()
Svc -> Repo : blocked either way?
alt blocked
  Svc --> WebA : 403
end
group «Unit of work» withTransaction()
  Svc -> Repo : save message, update conversation
  Repo -> DB : INSERT / UPDATE
end
Svc -> Bus : publish(B, "inbox")
note right of Bus : «Observer»
Bus --> WebB : event
WebB --> B : message + unread count
Ctrl --> WebA : sent

opt B reports the message
  B -> WebB : Report
  WebB -> Ctrl : POST /api/messages/conversations/:id/messages/:messageId/report
  Ctrl -> Svc : reportDirect()
  Svc -> Repo : support request for the admins (see diagram 11)
end
@enduml
